<title>ITALY: Italy's Bologna sees Dec CPI at 3.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Bologna sees Dec CPI at 3.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BOLOGNA, Italy 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Bologna said its December consumer price index stood at -0.3 percent month-on-month and 3.0 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In November, Bologna's inflation rate was 0.2 and 3.5 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Bologna is one of 10 Italian cities to publish inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.62 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to November 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		    -0.3   (0.2)     3.0  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.3  (-0.2)     1.5  (2.0)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0   (0.2)     2.4  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.1   (1.0)     6.6  (7.2)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (0.3)     1.5  (1.7)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0   (0.0)     5.0  (4.9)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.2   (0.3)     2.8  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -2.1   (0.1)     7.7 (10.1)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (1.5)     2.6  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.0)     2.6  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.1   (0.0)     0.8  (0.8)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
